# Build context filter for apps/server/Dockerfile and apps/web/Dockerfile
# (both are built from the repo root: docker build -f apps/<app>/Dockerfile .).
#
# Secrets: nothing secret may enter the build context, because anything in the
# context can end up in an image layer. The root .env points at the LIVE
# production database. Runtime configuration is injected by the orchestrator
# or secret manager at container start, never baked in.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.crt
# Public CA bundle the server uses to verify the managed Postgres pooler's
# certificate; it contains no private key.
!apps/server/certs/supabase-pooler-root.pem
.npmrc
**/.npmrc

# Dependencies and build output are produced inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.next-*
**/out
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo
.npm-cache
apps/server/generated

# Tests, reports, logs and review material are not part of any image.
apps/*/test
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/coverage
**/*.log
logs
review
graphify-out
**/*.md
.audit.json

# Tooling and VCS metadata.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.cursor
.claude
.vscode
.idea
supabase
scripts
docker-compose.yml
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
